id: 23
hanzi: 打猎
pinyin: dǎ liè
level: HSK 5
part_of_speech: Verb

meanings_summary:
  en: to go hunting; to chase and catch wild animals; venery
  es: cazar; ir de cacería; perseguir y abatir presas o piezas de caza

senses[1]{sense_number,part_of_speech,register,definition_en,definition_es,example_phrase}:
  1 | Verb | Standard | to pursue, chase, and shoot or capture wild animals or game for food, sport, or protection | perseguir y disparar a animales salvajes o presas para alimento, deporte o defensa | 上山打猎 (go up the mountain to hunt)

example_sentences[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 天色渐晚，李广将军率领随从在山林深处打猎，忽然发现前方草丛中似乎有一只猛虎正虎视眈眈。 | Tiānsè jiàn wǎn, Lǐ Guǎng jiāngjūn shuàilǐng suícóng zài shānlín shēnchù dǎliè, hūrán fāxiàn qiánfāng cǎocóng zhōng sìhū yǒu yì zhī měnghǔ zhèng hǔshì-dāndān. | As dusk deepened, General Li Guang led his retinue to hunt deep in mountain woods, when he suddenly spotted what seemed to be a fierce tiger glaring intently. | Caía la tarde cuando el general Li Guang y su séquito cazaban en la espesura del bosque, cuando divisó de improviso lo que parecía un tigre acechando entre la maleza.
  #2 | 为了保护珍稀濒危野生动物资源，国家自然保护区内严禁任何形式的非法打猎与盗伐林木行为。 | Wèile bǎohù zhēnxī bīnwēi yěshēng dòngwù zīyuán, guójiā zìrán bǎohùqū nèi yánjìn rènhé xíngshì de fēifǎ dǎliè yǔ dàofá línmù xíngwéi. | To protect rare and endangered wildlife resources, all forms of illegal hunting and unauthorized timber poaching are strictly banned in national reserves. | Para salvaguardar la fauna en peligro de extinción, en las reservas naturales nacionales queda tajantemente prohibida toda forma de caza furtiva o tala ilegal de árboles.

collocations[6]{hanzi,en}:
  上山打猎 | go into the mountains to hunt
  非法打猎 | illegal hunting; poaching
  打猎工具 | hunting gear or implements
  外出打猎 | go out on a hunt
  打猎猎犬 | hunting dog; hound
  打猎季节 | hunting season

idioms[4]{hanzi,pinyin,meaning_en}:
  打猎巡山 | dǎ liè xún shān | hunt and patrol the mountain forests
  引狼入室 | yǐn láng rù shì | lead a wolf into the house; invite disaster unwittingly
  如狼似虎 | rú láng sì hǔ | like wolves and tigers; ferocious and menacing
  草木皆兵 | cǎo mù jiē bīng | every bush and tree looks like an enemy soldier; state of extreme panic

character_decomposition[2]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,meaning_es,radical,radical_meaning_en,meaning_component,sound_component,stroke_count,composition_type,etymology_and_mnemonic,visual_mnemonic_story_en,visual_mnemonic_story_es,tone_mnemonic_anchor,cangjie,traditional}:
  打 | dǎ | strike; hit; beat; engage in | golpear; batir; emprender; cazar | 扌 | hand | 扌 (hand, physical strike) | 丁 (dīng, nail / phonetic) | 5 | 左右结构 | Phono-semantic compound: hand 扌 striking a nail or tool 丁. Extensively grammaticalized as a dynamic verb prefix. | A determined hand (扌) strikes down firmly like hammer on nail (丁) to perform an action (打). | Una mano decidida (扌) golpea con firmeza como martillo sobre clavo (丁) para emprender la acción (打). | 214 | QMN | 
  猎 | liè | hunt; chase game; pursue | cazar; perseguir presas | 犭 | dog / wild beast | 犭 (hunting hound / beast) | 昔 (xī, sun dried meat / past) | 11 | 左右结构 | Simplified from 獵. Ancient pictogram of hunting hounds 犭 racing through wild terrain to seize meat 昔. | An alert hunting dog (犭) dashes through golden autumn fields tracking game for dinner (昔) to hunt (猎). | Un fiel perro lebrel (犭) corretea ágil entre el matorral siguiendo el rastro de la caza (昔) para abatirla (猎). | 51 | KHTA | 獵

mnemonics_and_roots:
  composite_memory_hook_en: Striking with armed hands (打) alongside fierce hunting dogs tracking wild game (猎) captures the thrill of hunting (打猎).
  composite_memory_hook_es: Golpear con presteza (打) junto a lebreles de caza que persiguen a la fiera (猎) recrea la faena de cazar (打猎).
  cultural_and_cognitive_roots: In ancient China, imperial spring and autumn hunting expeditions (田猎) were sacred rituals testing martial readiness and horsemanship. Classical military strategy was intimately linked to tracking quarry in the wild, explaining why generals like Li Guang were consummate hunters.
  tone_sandhi_and_pitch_modulation: Dipping 3rd tone followed by falling 4th tone: 'dǎ liè' (214-51). Dip the pitch on 'dǎ' before striking firmly downward on 'liè'.

