    昔 | xī | past times; former days
    借 | jiè | borrow; lend
    惜 | xī | cherish; spare; begrudge

semantic_boundary_contrasts:
  core_nuance: 打猎 is the everyday verb phrase for hunting wildlife in forests and mountains.
  contrasts[3]{id,compared_word,pinyin,analysis}:
    1 | 打猎 vs. 捕鱼 | bǔyú | 打猎 focuses on terrestrial game, birds, and forest mammals using bows, guns, or traps, whereas 捕鱼 refers specifically to catching aquatic fish and crustaceans.
    2 | 打猎 vs. 盗猎 | dàoliè | 打猎 is a neutral historical or permitted sporting activity, whereas 盗猎 refers specifically to illegal poaching in violation of environmental laws.
    3 | 打猎 vs. 围猎 | wéiliè | 打猎 is generic hunting, whereas 围猎 denotes a large-scale collective battue or cordon hunt where troops encircle game.

extended_reading_passages[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 深秋的山林层林尽染，落叶在脚下发出沙沙的声响。猎人身背弓箭穿行在崇山峻岭之间，敏锐的双耳倾听着林间风吹草动的细微变化。古老的打猎生活不仅是对体魄的考验，更需要人与自然生态达成某种心照不宣的默契。 | Shēnqiū de shānlín cénglín-jìnrǎn, luòyè zài jiǎoxià fāchū shāshā de shēngxiǎng. Lièrén shēnbēi gōngjiàn chuānxíng zài chóngshān-jùnlǐng zhījiān, mǐnruì de shuāng'ěr qīngtīng zhe línjiān fēngchuī-cǎodòng de xìwēi biànhuà. Gǔlǎo de dǎliè shēnghuó bùjǐn shì duì tǐpò de kǎoyàn, gèng xūyào rén yǔ zìrán shēngtài dáchéng mǒuzhǒng xīnzhào-bùxuān de mòqì. | Late autumn woods glow with red leaves rustling underfoot. The hunter treks between rugged peaks with bow and arrow, ears alert to subtle changes in the breeze. Ancient hunting tested physical endurance and required tacit understanding with the mountain. | En otoño, las hojas caídas crujen bajo las pisadas en el bosque teñido de ocres. El cazador cruza riscos con su arco, atento al leve crujido de la hojarasca. Aquella ancestral vida de caza templaba el cuerpo y exigía una callada sintonía con las leyes del monte.
  #2 | 随着生态保护意识的不断增强，传统游猎民族的生活方式正在经历深刻转变。许多曾经世代依靠打猎为生的猎民主动收起猎枪，转而成为保护区里的护林员，用深沉的爱心守望着祖祖辈辈生活的莽莽林海。 | Suízhe shēngtài bǎohù yìshí de búduàn zēngqiáng, chuántǒng yóuliè mínzú de shēnghuó fāngshì zhèngzài jīnglì shēnkè zhuǎnbiàn. Xǔduō céngjīng shìdài yīkào dǎliè wéishēng de lièmín zhǔdòng shōuqǐ lièqiāng, zhuǎn'ér chéngwéi bǎohùqū lǐ de hùlínyuán, yòng shēnchén de àixīn shǒuwàng zhe zǔzǔ-bèibèi shēnghuó de mǎngmǎng línhǎi. | With burgeoning ecological awareness, nomadic hunting traditions are undergoing transformation. Many hunters who once subsisted on game voluntarily surrendered firearms to become rangers, safeguarding ancestral mountain forests with deep affection. | Al despertar la conciencia ecológica, los pueblos que vivían de la caza han transformado su modo de vida. Muchos cazadores han depuesto sus escopetas para convertirse en guardabosques de reservas naturales, custodiando con cariño la inmensidad forestal de sus ancestros.
